  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> Spell checking
  </title>
  <p>
    Orca can present spelling errors and suggestions while you use a supported application's
    spell checker.
  </p>
  <p>
    These features depend on accessibility information from the application or its toolkit that
    lets Orca recognize the misspelled word, suggestions list, and other parts of the
    spell-checking dialog. Orca currently recognizes these parts of the interface in some
    applications. If these features do not work in your application's spell checker, its
    interface may not yet be recognized, even if other parts of the application work well with
    Orca. Adding support may require changes in Orca, the application or its toolkit, or both.
  </p>
  <p>
    Even when an application's spell-checking dialog is not supported, Orca can announce
    misspelled words as you navigate or type. The application's spelling-error indicators,
    usually red squiggly underlines, must be enabled and exposed as accessibility text
    attributes. Announcements while typing also require the application to report changes to
    those attributes through accessibility events. Configure these announcements in "<link xref="features_speech_and_voices_verbosity#settings-verbosity">Verbosity preferences</link>".
  </p>
  <section id="settings-spell-checking">
    <title>Settings</title>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
      <gui>Spell Check</gui> category.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
    </p>
    <list>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Spell error</gui>: Controls whether Orca
          spells out the current error after speaking it. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Spell suggestion</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca spells out the current suggestion after speaking it. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
      <item>
        <p>
          <gui>Present context of error</gui>: Controls whether
          Orca presents the surrounding text in which the mistake occurred. Default: on.
        </p>
      </item>
    </list>
  </section>
